00:05:57.260 --> 00:06:00.000
I first heard about Miami Vice in October

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:04.280
I was being bi-coastal, I was going from Los Angeles to New York

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:07.680
and my agent calls me and says, "Philip, we've got a script

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:12.140
that we think is gonna be really good for you and we want you to read it and

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:15.420
they're gonna send it to me." So they sent it to me and I sat in New York

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:20.380
and I read this script and I said, "Wow, this is great." Written by Anthony Yurkovich.

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:24.230
Anthony Yurkovich. Wow! A couple years ago

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:27.160
I had done a guest shot on Starsky & Hutch

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:30.000
called Quadramania and I played this wild

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:34.640
Jamaican character. Kingston, St. Jacques, that voodoo doc with a cull from the hill turn

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:43.160
at 3 o'clock. And I said, hmm, okay, hmm. Then anyway, I got called in on it to an audition

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:49.660
and Milt Hammer was there and Anthony. And I said, I read the script and tell me about

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:54.790
it. And they said, well, it's going to be a video show, kind of a cop show, updated 80s

00:06:54.790 --> 00:07:00.000
kind of video show about drugs and stuff like that because of the things that go on in Miami

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:03.080
So I said, well, you know, I said, well, what are you looking for in terms of character?

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:06.080
Well, we don't know whether this is Tony talking.

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:09.200
We don't know whether we want it to be black or white or Spanish or what.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:11.200
But, you know, we're seeing everybody.

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:12.400
I said, well, listen, you don't have to look any further.

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:12.780
I'm it.

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:14.250
I am it.

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:16.570
You know, and he said, okay.

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:18.750
And I just had that particular meeting.

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:23.340
I get a call from my agent, and my agent says, your meeting went well, and everything is cool.

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:28.230
And so I go in, and I read with three different Crockett's, and I'm getting ready to leave.

00:07:28.370 --> 00:07:30.000
Bill Hammond runs to the elevator and says,

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:33.930
Philip, Philip, wait, we have one more person we want you to read with.

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:37.600
So I walk in, and all of NBC is there in the tower.

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:41.750
And Don Johnson is standing there.

00:07:41.930 --> 00:07:42.630
And I look at Don.

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:45.640
He looks at me, and he says, you guys want to read?

00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:48.590
I say, well, no, let's go for it.

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:49.120
Cold.

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:53.200
And all of a sudden, boom, it was like an explosive compulsion of a new affection.

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:53.700
Boom.

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:57.720
I mean, the energy that flowed in that room, everybody knew it.

00:07:57.800 --> 00:08:00.000
And when we were walking out, I said, in care

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.520
I said, "Man, you're gonna need me."

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:08.790
And the rest is history, what can I tell you?

