00:14:57.920 --> 00:14:59.830
and a couple of cars.

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:10.010
cars going by and rest is up to me sometimes i'll stop with drones i think of a rhythm sometimes i

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:16.330
don't even think of it it thinks of me you know it comes to me at uh sometimes very unopportune

00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:21.180
moments but i have to be ready for it and uh what i do is i usually program it into

00:15:21.180 --> 00:15:29.600
fairlight or limb sometimes it's a melody sometimes it's a complete piece of music

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:33.220
It's usually the best work that a composer can do, you know.

00:15:33.220 --> 00:15:38.710
It's really to be able to hear the whole piece enter your mind at once.

00:16:00.540 --> 00:16:06.370
There is an episode I'm working on right now, it's called Buddies, and it deals with best

00:16:06.370 --> 00:16:09.350
friend of Crockett's.

00:16:09.350 --> 00:16:17.260
Crockett saved his life in Vietnam, they're as close as people can get to a point where

00:16:17.260 --> 00:16:24.980
Crockett's friend Robbie wants Crockett to be his son's godfather.

00:16:24.980 --> 00:16:30.000
And Crockett is so close to this guy that he cannot see that this guy may be trapped

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:37.200
trouble. And Rico and Sonny are sitting in the car, and Tubs is trying to tell him, man,

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:42.510
you're really not seeing the thing clear. You're too blind to this. You know, this is

00:16:42.510 --> 00:16:42.810
trouble.

00:16:43.640 --> 00:16:44.900
